idinium-vilanterol 62.5/25 for management. He reports feeling well with no acute issues.\n\nJuly 3, 2022: Mr. Meyers was seen for his COPD management. His blood pressure was 106/78, and he weighed 101 pounds. His COPD continues to be well-controlled, with his FEV1 at 74% of the predicted value. He is using umeclidinium-vilanterol 62.5/25 as prescribed. He reports no issues, and his overall health remains stable.\n\nJanuary 11, 2022: Mr. Meyers visited for a routine COPD follow-up. His blood pressure was 109/77, and he weighed 101 pounds. His COPD is being managed effectively with umeclid"
